ion/math-academy-id "q-288406" :question/problem "The following equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\n$$\n-5{x}^{2}+mx-6=-5{x}^{2}-3x-6\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of the constant $m?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nWe compare the linear terms on both sides. On the left-hand side, the coefficient of $x$ is $m.$ On the right-hand side, the coefficient of $x$ is $-3.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nm=-3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-288406/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5cf64df7-0abb-5b42-bed6-b3664c2de89a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288406"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-288050"] :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nWe compare the linear terms on both sides. On the left-hand side, the coefficient of $x$ is $b.$ On the right-hand side, the coefficient of $x$ is $9.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nb=9.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-288448/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "d8d68d17-b4d2-5609-8bc9-032941933f05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288448/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "90b98ad6-0d26-5417-8a5f-23b1652dfcd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288448/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "0badedaf-efa3-504f-a7fa-bec469764e32" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-288448/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-288448/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-288448/field-1/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-288448" :question/id #uuid "77bcd568-42e4-5b14-ad02-144823509fd0" :question/math-academy-id "q-288448" :question/problem "The following equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\n$$\nk{x}^{2}+4x+1=-2{x}^{2}+4x+1\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of the constant $k?$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nWe compare the quadratic terms on both sides. On the left-hand side, the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is $k.$ On the right-hand side, the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is $-2.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nk=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-288448/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5cf64df7-0abb-5b42-bed6-b3664c2de89a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-288448"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-288446/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "0b7d2d19-dcd0-5314-b8b5-9fa26a34a163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288446/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "564bcc95-65a5-57d6-ae71-9e51a6c72a30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-288446/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "53aefaef-b653-5988-a27e-e1a4f42ff66b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answe